(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[10 1 "// memoryview's minimum (Objects/memoryobject.c), added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b): a view"] [11 1 "// of a bytes-like object's bytes, format 'B', one dimension: len, indexing and slicing, tobytes, tolist,"] [12 1 "// hex, release, the context manager, ==. _collections_abc registers the type at import. The buffer"] [13 1 "// protocol's other formats and shapes (cast, multi-dimensional views) are PY6's, with array and struct."] [17 1 "// MemoryView is a memoryview: its object, the start and length of its view, its step; released after"] [18 1 "// release()."] [23 24 "// \"\" is \"B\"; a cast's (PY6a): B b c H h I i L l Q q"] [24 2 "// PY7: exporter is the object a view of a class's __buffer__ (PEP 688) shows as obj (obj is then the view"] [25 2 "// __buffer__ returned); readonly a toreadonly's"] [28 2 "// mbuf is the export the view holds with the views made from it (queue 249, buffer_export.go): nil when its"] [29 2 "// exporter counts none"] [31 2 "// exports is the view's own (memory_getbuf's, and memory_hash's over the exporter's hash): release() refused while"] [32 2 "// any; hash once computed (queue 249)"] [36 2 "// shaped: the view is an exporter's PEP 3118 buffer (queue 260, BufferShaper: ctypes objects), its format, itemsize"] [37 2 "// isz and shape (ndim len(shape), 0 for a scalar) the exporter's, C-contiguous (start a byte offset, step 1)"] [41 2 "// st0 is a shaped view's first stride in bytes when a slice's step made it other than C's (queue 263: a step over a"] [42 2 "// dimension the slice leaves at most one long, the view still C-contiguous); 0 is C's"] [46 1 "// BufferShaper is an exporter whose buffer is not a 1-D array of bytes (queue 260): Py_buffer's format, itemsize and"] [47 1 "// shape (ndim its length; strides NULL, so C-contiguous) as its getbufferproc gives them, ctypes' PyCData_NewGetBuffer."] [48 1 "// memoryview(o) of such an o is a view of that shape; its bytes are o's BytesLike, written through WritableBytes."] [53 1 "// shaperOf is o's BufferShaper (or its built-in value's), nil when o's buffer is plain bytes."] [64 1 "// viewOf is o's buffer described as a view (PyObject_GetBuffer): o itself when a memoryview, nil when no buffer."] [81 1 "// shapeList is view->shape."] [89 1 "// structFmt reports whether the struct module unpacks f (struct_get_unpacker): its byte orders, counts and codes only."] [99 1 "// ndim is view->ndim."] [107 1 "// nativeFmt is adjust_fmt's get_native_fmtstr for a shaped view: its format as a native single character ('@'"] [108 1 "// dropped), else NotImplementedError (ctypes' \"<i\", \"T{...}\": the struct module's, not memoryview's)."] [117 1 "// shapedList is tolist of a shaped view's dimension d at byte offset off (tolist_rec)."] [119 30 "// unpack_single: the format's own size"] [121 34 "// an item past a buffer of size 0 (an incomplete structure's \"B\"): CPython reads its zeroed b_value"] [137 1 "// shapedGet is memory_subscript of a shaped view."] [170 18 "// init_slice: strides[0] *= step"] [176 2 "// an index (memory_item), a tuple of indices (memory_item_multi), a tuple of slices, else invalid"] [237 1 "// stride0 is a shaped view's first stride in bytes (view->strides[0])."] [249 1 "// shapedSetND is memory_ass_sub of a shaped view of more than one dimension (queue 263, a cast's): a full tuple of"] [250 1 "// indices packs one item (ptr_from_tuple, pack_single); an index, a shorter tuple or a slice is not implemented."] [301 1 "// packAt is pack_single of v into a shaped view's item at byte offset off: the byte formats (pyi's shaped views pack"] [302 1 "// no wider item yet)."] [304 18 "// queue 286: pack_single's wider formats"] [319 13 "// pack_single's byte formats: type_error_int, value_error_int"] [356 1 "// mvPlainByte: the format is 'B' (or none, a plain view's), whose items the byte paths index."] [359 1 "// multiGet is memory_subscript of a 1-D view of a format wider than a byte (a cast's, unshaped; queue 286): an"] [360 1 "// index's item (unpack_single), a slice's view of the same format, its items step apart (init_slice)."] [396 1 "// multiSet is memory_ass_sub of a 1-D view of format f, items sz bytes wide, cnt of them, st bytes apart (queue 286):"] [397 1 "// an index packs one item (pack_single), a slice copies a view of the same structure (equiv_structure, copy_single)."] [453 1 "// mvPack is pack_single (Objects/memoryobject.c) of v into b, one item of native format f (queue 286): the integer"] [454 1 "// formats by __index__ (type_error_int, value_error_int), the floats by PyFloat_AsDouble, '?' by truth, 'c' one byte;"] [455 1 "// fix_error_int's messages for the conversions' errors."] [545 12 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr: a negative pointer as PyLong_AsLongLong's"] [551 11 "// B H I L Q N"] [561 1 "// derive registers nv, a view made from m (a slice, a cast, memoryview(m), toreadonly), with m's managed buffer."] [567 1 "// exportedObj is the view's obj attribute: the exporter's object."] [575 1 "// mvFlagsFullRO is PyBUF_FULL_RO, the flags memoryview() and bytes() ask a __buffer__ for."] [578 1 "// bufferOf is a class's __buffer__(flags): its memoryview, nil when the type has none (PY7: memoryview() and bytes()"] [579 1 "// of such an object raised TypeError)."] [600 1 "// ExtBufferHook is the buffer of an object whose type a C extension made with bf_getbuffer (arbace/pyctypes, queue"] [601 1 "// 270b): its view (found false when the type has none), as bufferOf's of a class's __buffer__."] [604 1 "// NewBytesView is a memoryview of the bytes b (format 'B'), read-only when readonly, for ExtBufferHook's views."] [609 1 "// releaseBuffer is PyBuffer_Release of a view bufferOf got: the exporter's __release_buffer__(view), when it has one."] [618 1 "// release is memoryview.release(): the exporter's buffer released once."] [640 1 "// mvItemSizes are get_native_fmtchar's formats and their native sizes (64-bit Linux; queue 263: n N f d e ? P too)."] [644 1 "// mvFmtChar is a native single-character format without its optional '@' (get_native_fmtchar's character)."] [652 1 "// mvFmtSize is get_native_fmtchar: a native format's item size, false when f is none (3.15.2: also \"Zf\" and \"Zd\","] [653 1 "// the complex formats; 3.14.10: one character only)."] [668 1 "// mvByteFmt is IS_BYTE_FORMAT of a view's format: 'b', 'B' or 'c', with an optional '@'."] [685 1 "// item is the i-th item of a cast view: little-endian, signed for the lower-case formats."] [690 54 "// queue 263: unpack_single's other native formats, as the struct module's"] [691 31 "// 3.15.2's complexes: the struct module's F and D, native"] [724 62 "// queue 286: a strided slice of a cast view, item by item"] [740 1 "// BytesLike makes a memoryview a bytes-like object (asBytes): a copy of its bytes."] [754 4 "// a view of a view: the same buffer, start, length and stride (CPython's memory_from_buffer keeps the"] [755 4 "// strides, so a non-contiguous view stays one)"] [762 42 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [776 4 "// the export of a class's __buffer__: its __release_buffer__ called when the last view goes"] [785 40 "// queue 260: the exporter's format, itemsize and shape"] [791 2 "// memory_hash (queue 249): a read-only byte view's hash is its bytes' (hash(b'..')), the exporter hashed first with"] [792 2 "// the view exported meanwhile (gh-142664: a re-entrant __hash__ that releases the view gets BufferError)"] [853 61 "// queue 286: a cast view's items (multiprocessing's Barrier: cast('i'))"] [876 2 "// item and slice assignment into a writable buffer (PY6d's REQUEST: _pyio's readinto, pickle's protocol 5"] [877 2 "// bytearray); byte views only"] [890 17 "// queue 260: a shaped view's items are the struct module's formats (memory_ass_sub's adjust_fmt)"] [902 27 "// queue 263: a 0-dim view's one item (a cast to shape ())"] [905 20 "// queue 286: a 1-D view of a wider format"] [910 62 "// queue 286: a cast view's items (multiprocessing's Barrier: cast('i'), '?', 'b', 'c')"] [975 3 "// queue 260 (memory_richcompare): views of other shapes differ (equiv_shape), and a format the struct module"] [976 3 "// cannot unpack (\"T{...}\", \"&<i\", \"<O\") makes the views unequal, a view itself included"] [1011 17 "// queue 260: tolist_rec over the exporter's shape, native formats only (adjust_fmt)"] [1032 2 "// cast (queue 263): memoryview_cast_impl over cast_to_1D and cast_to_ND, Objects/memoryobject.c (3.14.10): the"] [1033 2 "// format, then a shape of any number of dimensions (1D -> ND or ND -> 1D); the result a view of the same memory"] [1053 74 "// MV_C_CONTIGUOUS"] [1081 3 "// cast_to_1D"] [1094 18 "// not a native single character: not a byte format"] [1103 3 "// a strided view of at most one item is C-contiguous: the cast's view starts at its item, step 1"] [1105 21 "// cast_to_ND: copy_shape, then the buffer's size"] [1141 2 "// count, index and toreadonly (PY7: absent): over tolist's items, as memory_count and memory_index"] [1153 81 "// queue 263: memory_iter's checks"] [1179 81 "// queue 263: memoryview_index_impl's"] [1223 3 "// a 1-D view's shape, strides and contiguity (PY7: absent)"] [1235 18 "// C-contiguous: init_strides_from_shape"] [1264 34 "// CHECK_RELEASED (PY7: obj stayed readable; no attribute \"released\", CPython's has none)"] [1272 1 "// unusable is the view's CHECK_RELEASED, and its exporter's own check when it has one (queue 204: an mmap closed under"] [1273 1 "// the view raises ValueError \"mmap closed or invalid\", where CPython's mmap refuses the close; pyi counts no exports)."] [1284 1 "// isReadonly is view->readonly: a toreadonly's or __buffer__'s view, or one of an exporter that is not writable (queue 249:"] [1285 1 "// an array's buffer is writable, as arraymodule.c exports it; only a bytearray's was before)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[55 30] [58 44] [66 29] [74 22] [111 26] [140 25] [156 25] [179 24] [182 28] [185 26] [197 33] [252 24] [2